IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgd-amalgamation`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- amalgamation (ss 215A to 215H, with the short form of s 215D) as ONE CHAIN of steps, a regulative layer over the Boolean encoding in sgd-amalgamation.l4.
-- The gates are the existing section functions, called and not restated: s 215D(1) and s 215D(2) (whether the short form applies), s 215E(1) (whether the documents filed are those the subsection requires),
-- s 215H(1) (whether the Court may make an order). The existing DEONTIC rules of sgd-amalgamation.l4 are not called: the chain is written again from the text.
-- The chain, each clock measured from its own trigger: before the general meeting, the board resolves and makes the solvency statements (s 215C(2)); not less than 21 days before the meeting the board sends the proposal
-- and the declarations to every member (s 215C(4)) and the directors send the proposal to every secured creditor and publish the notice (s 215C(5)); in the short form the directors give written notice to every secured creditor
-- not less than 21 days before the meeting (s 215D(3)) and the board makes the solvency statement before the meeting begins (s 215D(5)); the members approve by special resolution at the meeting (ss 215C(1)(a), 215D(1));
-- the documents are filed with the Registrar (s 215E(1)); the Registrar issues the notice of amalgamation (s 215F(1)), removes the amalgamating companies from the register (s 215F(3)) and, on application, issues the certificate (s 215F(4));
-- the amalgamation takes effect on the date shown in the notice (s 215G, no duty: its date ends the Court window); a member, creditor or person owed an obligation may apply to the Court before that date (s 215H(1)).
-- Every deadline in this chain is a backward count from a date the caller supplies (the meeting, or the date of effect), or has no number at all, so a TRACE has no calendar of its own: each DATE input must agree with
-- the day of the trace on which that event happens, and day 0 of every trace is the start day of the trace (the first day on which any step of the chain is open).
-- Parties are the corpus's own `Party` (sg-core.l4). Where a step is a power with a time limit (MAY ... WITHIN), a missed limit is not a breach: the text states no consequence except that the power is gone, so LEST is FULFILLED.
-- Where a step is a duty with no number of days in the text, it takes the found period of the section modules as a rule-level input: `the period of all convenient speed, as found` where the text states no time (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52), and `the period the standard of time allows, as found` where the section's own standard of time governs ("as soon as practicable", s 215F(3)); the inputs are numbers of days found by whoever applies the rule, with no default (decided, assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
-- Two duties are left without a clock, and so without a LEST: the filing of s 215E(1) (the text names no one who must file, and a breach by a party the text does not name would be invented) and the notice of s 215F(1)(b) (the existing rule of sgd-amalgamation.l4 carries no LEST for it either).
-- Convention for the procedure layer (assumed, not ruled): BREACH is kept only for a duty or a prohibition that the text lays on a named party; a power that lapses unused, a condition that is not met, a vote that fails and a route that has closed end FULFILLED.

DECLARE `amalgamation chain act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215C(2)(a) the board resolves that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company`
    `s 215C(2)(b) the board makes the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company`
    `s 215C(2)(c) the board makes the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company`
    `s 215C(3) the director signs the declaration`
    `s 215C(4) the board sends the proposal, the declarations, the statement of interests and the further information to every member`
    `s 215C(5)(a) the directors send the proposal to every secured creditor`
    `s 215C(5)(b) the directors cause the notice to be published in a daily English newspaper`
    `s 215C(1)(a) the members approve the amalgamation proposal by special resolution at a general meeting`
    `s 215D(3) the directors give written notice of the proposed amalgamation to every secured creditor`
    `s 215D(5) the board makes the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company`
    `s 215D(6) the director signs the declaration`
    `s 215D(1) the members resolve by special resolution at a general meeting to approve the amalgamation on the terms`
    `s 215E(1) the amalgamating company files the documents with the Registrar with the prescribed fee`
    `s 215F(1)(a) the Registrar issues the notice of amalgamation`
    `s 215F(1)(b) the Registrar issues the notice of amalgamation together with the notice of incorporation`
    `s 215F(3) the Registrar removes the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register`
    `s 215F(4) the amalgamated company applies for a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation`
    `s 215F(4) the Registrar issues the certificate of confirmation of amalgamation`
    `s 215H(1) the person applies to the Court`
    `s 215H(1)(a) the Court directs that effect must not be given to the amalgamation proposal`
    `s 215H(1)(b) the Court modifies the amalgamation proposal`
    `s 215H(1)(c) the Court directs the amalgamating company or its board to reconsider the amalgamation proposal`
    `s 215H(1) the Court makes any other order it thinks fit in relation to the amalgamation proposal`

§ `Helpers: deadlines turned into days`

-- "before the general meeting": the last day is the day before the meeting (sg-periods P1 on the latest day an act can be before a date); an act on the day of the meeting is not counted as before it (fork below).
GIVEN `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day before the general meeting` MEANS
    (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the general meeting` 1 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- "not less than 21 days before the general meeting": the last day is the day 21 days before the meeting.
GIVEN `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the last day not less than 21 days before the general meeting` MEANS
    (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the general meeting` 21 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- "before the commencement of the general meeting": the last day is the day of the meeting itself, because a date does not say at what hour the meeting began (fork below).
GIVEN `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day of the general meeting` MEANS
    `the day of the general meeting` MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- "at any time before the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective": the last day is the day before the date of effect.
GIVEN `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day before the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` MEANS
    (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` 1 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

§ `Section 215C: the duties of the board and the directors before the general meeting (the long form)`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the start day of the trace; counting="before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a)" for the board's resolution and the two solvency statements (the last day is the day before the meeting, from the DATE input of the meeting); "not less than 21 days before the general meeting" for sending to every member, to every secured creditor, and publishing the notice (the last day is the meeting day less 21 days); the director's declaration has no day in the text (silent)
-- FORK: s 215C(2) | an act on the day of the meeting is not "before the general meeting": the last day is the day before the meeting, as the existing function `s 215C(2) the number of days from the start day to the day before the general meeting` reads it | an act on the day of the meeting but before it starts, which a date alone cannot place
-- FORK: s 215C(3) | the declaration is a duty of each director who votes in favour with no last day, because subsection (3) names none; subsection (4)(b) requires a copy of the declarations to be sent not less than 21 days before the meeting, which implies they exist by then, but that is not a time limit on the signing | the signing as due by the last day for the sending under subsection (4)
-- FORK: s 215C(2) | the duties before the meeting are owed from day 0 on the assumption that the amalgamation proposal goes to the general meeting: a board that decides against the amalgamation, and so never calls the meeting, is shown in breach on the day before the meeting date the caller supplies | a gate on an input that the meeting is held on the proposal
-- FORK: s 215C(3), s 215D(6) | the declaration is a duty of each director who votes in favour, and the text gives it no number of days, so the period is the found input of the section module (sgd-amalgamation.l4:1197-1203, 1333-1339); a late signing is a BREACH by the director | no clock, as the signing stood before the review
-- FORK: s 215C(4), (5) | "not less than 21 days before" is read as: the last day is the meeting day less 21 days, and an act on that day is in time (sg-periods) | the day before it
-- FORK: s 215C(5) | "the directors ... must" is encoded as a duty of one named director, one rule each for sending and for publishing | a joint duty of every director
-- Offence (s 215C(6) "Any director who contravenes subsection (3) shall be guilty of an offence"): the text gives subsection (3) no last day and subsection (6) no penalty, so no step of the trace is the contravention and none is encoded.
-- src:21175 | (2) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
-- src:21176 | before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21178 | (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the
-- src:21179 | amalgamating company;
-- src:21181 | (b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating
-- src:21182 | company in accordance with section 215I; and
-- src:21184 | (c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated
-- src:21185 | company in accordance with section 215J.
-- src:21190 | (3) Every director who votes in favour of the resolution and the
-- src:21191 | making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2) must sign a
-- src:21192 | declaration stating —
-- src:21194 | (a) that, in his or her opinion, the conditions specified in
-- src:21195 | subsection (2)(a), section 215I(1)(a) and (b) (in relation to
-- src:21196 | the amalgamating company) and section 215J(1)(a) and (b)
-- src:21197 | (in relation to the amalgamated company) are satisfied; and
-- src:21199 | (b) the grounds for that opinion.
-- src:21201 | (4) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must
-- src:21202 | send to every member of the amalgamating company, not less than
-- src:21203 | 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21205 | (a) a copy of the amalgamation proposal;
-- src:21207 | (b) a copy of the declarations given by the directors under
-- src:21208 | subsection (3);
-- src:21210 | (c) a statement of any material interests of the directors,
-- src:21211 | whether in that capacity or otherwise; and
-- src:21213 | (d) such further information and explanation as may be
-- src:21214 | necessary to enable a reasonable member of the
-- src:21215 | amalgamating company to understand the nature and
-- src:21216 | implications, for the amalgamating company and its
-- src:21217 | members, of the proposed amalgamation.
-- src:21219 | (5) The directors of each amalgamating company must, not less
-- src:21220 | than 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in
-- src:21221 | subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21223 | (a) send a copy of the amalgamation proposal to every secured
-- src:21224 | creditor of the amalgamating company; and
-- src:21226 | (b) cause to be published in at least one daily English
-- src:21227 | newspaper circulating generally in Singapore a notice of
-- src:21228 | the proposed amalgamation, including a statement that —
-- src:21230 | (i) copies of the amalgamation proposal are available
-- src:21231 | for inspection by any member or creditor of an
-- src:21232 | amalgamating company at the registered offices of
-- src:21233 | the amalgamating companies and at such other place
-- src:21238 | as may be specified in the notice during ordinary
-- src:21239 | business hours; and
-- src:21241 | (ii) a member or creditor of an amalgamating company is
-- src:21242 | entitled to be supplied free of charge with a copy of
-- src:21243 | the amalgamation proposal upon request to an
-- src:21244 | amalgamating company.
@ref s 215C(2) to (5) the duties of the board and the directors before the general meeting (src:21175-21244)
GIVEN `the name of the amalgamating company` IS A STRING
      `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215C chain: the duties before the general meeting` MEANS
    (PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company`
     MUST `s 215C(2)(a) the board resolves that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company`
     WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day before the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not resolve before the general meeting that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company")
    RAND
    ((PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company`
      MUST `s 215C(2)(b) the board makes the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company`
      WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day before the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
      HENCE FULFILLED
      LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company before the general meeting")
     RAND
     ((PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company`
       MUST `s 215C(2)(c) the board makes the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company`
       WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day before the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
       HENCE FULFILLED
       LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company before the general meeting")
      RAND
      ((PARTY Director `the name of the director`
        MUST `s 215C(3) the director signs the declaration`
        WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (decided, assumed, not ruled; s 215C(3); see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not sign a declaration stating that, in the director's opinion, the conditions are satisfied, and the grounds for that opinion (s 215C(3))")
       RAND
       ((PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company`
         MUST `s 215C(4) the board sends the proposal, the declarations, the statement of interests and the further information to every member`
         WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the last day not less than 21 days before the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not send what subsection (4) requires to every member not less than 21 days before the general meeting")
        RAND
        ((PARTY Director `the name of the director`
          MUST `s 215C(5)(a) the directors send the proposal to every secured creditor`
          WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the last day not less than 21 days before the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "a copy of the amalgamation proposal was not sent to every secured creditor not less than 21 days before the general meeting")
         RAND
         (PARTY Director `the name of the director`
          MUST `s 215C(5)(b) the directors cause the notice to be published in a daily English newspaper`
          WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the last day not less than 21 days before the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "a notice of the proposed amalgamation was not published not less than 21 days before the general meeting"))))))

§ `Section 215D: the duties of the directors and the board before the general meeting (the short form)`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the start day of the trace; counting="not less than 21 days before the general meeting" for the written notice to every secured creditor (the last day is the meeting day less 21 days); "before the commencement of the general meeting" for the solvency statement (the last day is the meeting day, because a date does not say at what hour it began); the director's declaration has no day in the text (silent)
-- FORK: s 215D(5) | "before the commencement of the general meeting" is read as due by the end of the meeting day, since an act on that day may precede the start, and a date cannot tell | the day before the meeting, as the existing DEONTIC reads it
-- FORK: s 215D(6) | the declaration is a duty of each director who votes in favour of the statement, with no last day, because subsection (6) names none | a last day at the meeting
-- Offence (s 215D(7) "Any director who contravenes subsection (6) shall be guilty of an offence"): subsection (6) has no last day and subsection (7) no penalty, so no step of the trace is the contravention and none is encoded.
-- src:21326 | (3) The directors of each amalgamating company must, not less
-- src:21327 | than 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)
-- src:21328 | or (2) (as the case may be) give written notice of the proposed
-- src:21333 | amalgamation to every secured creditor of the amalgamating
-- src:21334 | company.
-- src:21336 | (4) The resolution mentioned in subsection (1) or (2) (as the case
-- src:21337 | may be) is deemed to be an amalgamation proposal that has been
-- src:21338 | approved.
-- src:21340 | (5) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
-- src:21341 | before the commencement of the general meeting mentioned in
-- src:21342 | subsection (1) or (2) (as the case may be), make a solvency statement
-- src:21343 | in relation to the amalgamated company in accordance with
-- src:21344 | section 215J.
-- src:21348 | (6) Every director who votes in favour of the making of the
-- src:21349 | solvency statement mentioned in subsection (5) must sign a
-- src:21350 | declaration stating —
-- src:21352 | (a) that, in the director’s opinion, the conditions specified in
-- src:21353 | section 215J(1)(a) and (b) are satisfied; and
-- src:21355 | (b) the grounds for that opinion.
-- src:21357 | (7) Any director who contravenes subsection (6) shall be guilty of
-- src:21358 | an offence.
@ref s 215D(3) to (7) the duties of the directors and the board before the general meeting (src:21326-21358)
GIVEN `the name of the amalgamating company` IS A STRING
      `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215D chain: the duties before the general meeting` MEANS
    (PARTY Director `the name of the director`
     MUST `s 215D(3) the directors give written notice of the proposed amalgamation to every secured creditor`
     WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the last day not less than 21 days before the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "written notice of the proposed amalgamation was not given to every secured creditor not less than 21 days before the general meeting")
    RAND
    ((PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company`
      MUST `s 215D(5) the board makes the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company`
      WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day of the general meeting` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace`)
      HENCE FULFILLED
      LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company before the commencement of the general meeting")
     RAND
     (PARTY Director `the name of the director`
      MUST `s 215D(6) the director signs the declaration`
     WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (decided, assumed, not ruled; s 215D(6); see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not sign the declaration (s 215D(6))"))

§ `Sections 215E to 215G: the filing, the Registrar's notice, the removal from the register and the certificate`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the start day of the trace; counting: the filing "must be filed" has no day and no named bearer, so no clock is encoded for it; the Registrar acts "upon the receipt" (s 215F(1)(a), the found period of all convenient speed, running from the filing), "as soon as practicable after the effective date" (s 215F(3), the found period of the standard of time, running from the Registrar's notice) and "upon the application" (s 215F(4), the found period of all convenient speed, running from the application); each step is reached by HENCE from the step before it
-- FORK: s 215E(1) | the text says the documents "must be filed" without naming who files them; the amalgamating company is the party, and the documents it files are the ones the existing gate `s 215E(1) the documents filed with the Registrar are those the subsection requires` approves | the directors, or each amalgamating company
-- FORK: s 215E(1), 215F(1) | a filing that lacks what the subsection requires is not "the relevant documents", so the Registrar's duty has not arisen and the company's duty to file stays open; a second filing is assumed to be complete | the Registrar issuing the notice regardless
-- FORK: s 215F(4) | the application for the certificate is a power of the amalgamated company with no last day, and the certificate a duty of the Registrar once the application is made | a duty of the Registrar to issue the certificate without an application
-- FORK: s 215F(3) | the text runs "as soon as practicable" from the effective date, but the rule is reached by HENCE from the Registrar's notice and does not know the effective date, so the found period runs from the notice; the caller finds the period with that in mind | the period running from the effective date
-- FORK: s 215F(1)(b) | the notice of amalgamation with the notice of incorporation is left without a clock, as the existing rule is (sgd-amalgamation.l4:1356-1360, class "other" in notes/lest-without-deadline.md); the (a) form takes the period of all convenient speed | a clock for the (b) form too
-- FORK: s 215E(1) | the filing is left without a clock and a LEST: the text names no one who must file (see the fork above), so a breach by the amalgamating company would be invented | the found period of all convenient speed and a breach by the amalgamating company
-- s 215G itself imposes no duty (the amalgamation is effective, the name, property and liabilities pass on "the date shown in a notice of amalgamation"): it is carried by the DATE input that ends the Court's window below, and by the existing function `s 215G on the date shown in the notice of amalgamation the effect has taken place`.
-- src:21365 | 215E.—(1) For the purpose of effecting an amalgamation, the
-- src:21366 | following documents must be filed with the Registrar, in the
-- src:21367 | prescribed form with such particulars as may be required in the
-- src:21368 | form, together with payment of the prescribed fee:
-- src:21421 | 215F.—(1) Upon the receipt of the relevant documents and fees,
-- src:21422 | the Registrar must —
-- src:21424 | (a) if the amalgamated company is the same as one of the
-- src:21425 | amalgamating companies — issue a notice of
-- src:21426 | amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may
-- src:21427 | determine; or
-- src:21432 | (b) if the amalgamated company is a new company — issue a
-- src:21433 | notice of amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may
-- src:21434 | determine together with the notice of incorporation under
-- src:21435 | section 19(4).
-- src:21445 | (3) The Registrar must, as soon as practicable after the effective
-- src:21446 | date of an amalgamation, remove the amalgamating companies, other
-- src:21447 | than the amalgamated company, from the register.
-- src:21449 | (4) Upon the application of the amalgamated company and
-- src:21450 | payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the
-- src:21451 | amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of
-- src:21452 | amalgamation.
-- src:21458 | 215G. On the date shown in a notice of amalgamation —
-- src:21460 | (a) the amalgamation is effective;
@ref s 215E(1) to s 215G the filing, the notice, the removal, the certificate and the effect (src:21365-21460)
GIVEN `the amalgamating company as a party` IS A Party
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as practicable") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215F chain: the removal from the register and the certificate of confirmation` MEANS
    (PARTY Registrar
     MUST `s 215F(3) the Registrar removes the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register`
     WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "as soon as practicable" (s 215F(3)); the period is an input, as found (decided, assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
     HENCE FULFILLED
     LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not remove the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register (s 215F(3))")
    RAND
    (PARTY `the amalgamating company as a party`
     MAY `s 215F(4) the amalgamated company applies for a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation`
     HENCE (PARTY Registrar
            MUST `s 215F(4) the Registrar issues the certificate of confirmation of amalgamation`
            WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (decided, assumed, not ruled; s 215F(4); see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue to the amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation (s 215F(4))"))

GIVEN `the amalgamating company as a party` IS A Party
      `the amalgamated company is a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as practicable") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215F chain: the notice of amalgamation` MEANS
    IF `the amalgamated company is a new company`
    THEN (PARTY Registrar
          MUST `s 215F(1)(b) the Registrar issues the notice of amalgamation together with the notice of incorporation`
          HENCE (`s 215F chain: the removal from the register and the certificate of confirmation` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`))
    ELSE (PARTY Registrar
          MUST `s 215F(1)(a) the Registrar issues the notice of amalgamation`
          WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (decided, assumed, not ruled; s 215F(1)(a); see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
          HENCE (`s 215F chain: the removal from the register and the certificate of confirmation` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`)
          LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue a notice of amalgamation (s 215F(1)(a))")

GIVEN `the amalgamating company as a party` IS A Party
      `the amalgamated company is a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as practicable") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215E chain: the filing with the Registrar, then the Registrar's notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the amalgamating company as a party`
    MUST `s 215E(1) the amalgamating company files the documents with the Registrar with the prescribed fee`
    HENCE (IF `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN (`s 215F chain: the notice of amalgamation` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the amalgamated company is a new company` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`)
           ELSE (PARTY `the amalgamating company as a party`
                 MUST `s 215E(1) the amalgamating company files the documents with the Registrar with the prescribed fee`
                 HENCE (`s 215F chain: the notice of amalgamation` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the amalgamated company is a new company` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`)))

§ `Section 215H(1): the application to the Court before the amalgamation becomes effective`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the start day of the trace; counting="at any time before the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective" (the last day is the day before the date of effect, from the DATE input of that date; the text names no day on which the window opens, so it is open from day 0); the Court's power has no limit of time in the text (silent)
-- FORK: s 215H(1) | the application is a MAY of the person with a limit, and a missed limit ends the power with nothing owed (FULFILLED); the Court's power to order is a MAY of the Court with no limit, and each of the orders in paragraphs (a) to (c) and "any order it thinks fit" is one alternative | the Court's inaction as a refusal
-- FORK: s 215H(1) | where the Court is not satisfied that giving effect to the proposal would unfairly prejudice the person, or the applicant is not within the three kinds the subsection names, or the application is not before the date of effect, the existing gate does not answer JUST TRUE and the Court has no power to order: the chain ends with nothing owed | a refusal as a step
-- FORK: s 215H(1) | what an order under paragraph (a), (b) or (c) does to the filing and the Registrar's steps is not stated in the text, so no order stops or changes them in this encoding (the existing Boolean layer carries no such rule either)
-- FORK: s 215H(1) | the date of effect is a DATE input (the date specified in the proposal under s 215B(2), or the date shown in the notice under s 215G); the Registrar's notice may set it after the application is made, and the trace cannot compute it from the Registrar's step
-- src:21491 | 215H.—(1) If the Court is satisfied that giving effect to an
-- src:21492 | amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice a member or
-- src:21493 | creditor of an amalgamating company or a person to whom an
-- src:21494 | amalgamating company is under an obligation, it may, on the
-- src:21495 | application of that person made at any time before the date on which
-- src:21496 | the amalgamation becomes effective, make any order it thinks fit in
-- src:21497 | relation to the amalgamation proposal, and may, without limiting the
-- src:21498 | generality of this subsection, make an order —
-- src:21500 | (a) directing that effect must not be given to the amalgamation
-- src:21501 | proposal;
-- src:21503 | (b) modifying the amalgamation proposal in such manner as
-- src:21504 | may be specified in the order; or
-- src:21506 | (c) directing the amalgamating company or its board of
-- src:21507 | directors to reconsider the amalgamation proposal or any
-- src:21508 | part thereof.
-- src:21510 | (2) An order may be made under subsection (1) on such terms or
-- src:21511 | conditions as the Court thinks fit.
@ref s 215H(1), (2) the Court's power to make an order before the date of effect (src:21491-21511)
GIVEN `the person who applies` IS A Party
      `what the person who applies is` IS A `s 215H(1) the person`
      `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application to the Court` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215H chain: the application to the Court, then the order` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who applies`
    MAY `s 215H(1) the person applies to the Court`
    WITHIN (`s 215 chain: the days from the start day to the day before the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` `the start day of the trace`)
    HENCE (IF (`s 215H(1) the Court may make an order in relation to the amalgamation proposal` `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` `what the person who applies is` TRUE `the day of the application to the Court` `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
           THEN ((PARTY Court
                  MAY `s 215H(1)(a) the Court directs that effect must not be given to the amalgamation proposal`
                  HENCE FULFILLED)
                 ROR
                 ((PARTY Court
                   MAY `s 215H(1)(b) the Court modifies the amalgamation proposal`
                   HENCE FULFILLED)
                  ROR
                  ((PARTY Court
                    MAY `s 215H(1)(c) the Court directs the amalgamating company or its board to reconsider the amalgamation proposal`
                    HENCE FULFILLED)
                   ROR
                   (PARTY Court
                    MAY `s 215H(1) the Court makes any other order it thinks fit in relation to the amalgamation proposal`
                    HENCE FULFILLED))))
           ELSE FULFILLED)
    LEST FULFILLED

§ `Sections 215C(1)(a) and 215D(1): the members' resolution, with what follows it`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the start day of the trace; counting=silent for the resolution itself ("by special resolution at a general meeting", with no last day: the text fixes the meeting only as the point the board's duties above are measured from); the steps after it are as in the sections above
-- FORK: s 215C(1)(a), 215D(1) | the members' resolution is a MAY of the members with no limit, and its HENCE is the filing: the filing is not open before the resolution | the filing as a duty open from day 0
-- FORK: s 215C(1)(b) | the approval "by any other person, where any provision in the amalgamation proposal would ... require the approval of that person" is not encoded: the text names no person | an extra step
-- FORK: s 215D(4) | "the resolution ... is deemed to be an amalgamation proposal that has been approved": the short-form resolution leads to the filing as the long-form resolution does
-- src:21161 | 215C.—(1) An amalgamation proposal must be approved —
-- src:21163 | (a) subject to the constitution of each amalgamating company,
-- src:21164 | by the members of each amalgamating company by special
-- src:21165 | resolution at a general meeting; and
-- src:21167 | (b) by any other person, where any provision in the
-- src:21168 | amalgamation proposal would, if contained in any
-- src:21169 | amendment to the constitution of an amalgamating
-- src:21170 | company or otherwise proposed in relation to that
-- src:21171 | company, require the approval of that person.
-- src:21251 | 215D.—(1) A company (called in this subsection the amalgamating
-- src:21252 | holding company) and one or more of its wholly‑owned subsidiaries
-- src:21253 | (called in this subsection the amalgamating subsidiary company) may
-- src:21254 | amalgamate and continue as one company, being the amalgamated
-- src:21255 | holding company or the amalgamated subsidiary company, without
-- src:21256 | complying with sections 215B and 215C if the members of each
-- src:21257 | amalgamating company, by special resolution at a general meeting,
-- src:21258 | resolve to approve an amalgamation of the amalgamating companies
-- src:21259 | on the terms that —
@ref s 215C(1), s 215D(1) the members' resolution (src:21161-21259)
GIVEN `the short form applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members as a party` IS A Party
      `the amalgamating company as a party` IS A Party
      `the amalgamated company is a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person who applies` IS A Party
      `what the person who applies is` IS A `s 215H(1) the person`
      `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application to the Court` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as practicable") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215 chain: the members' resolution, the filing, the Registrar's steps and the Court's power` MEANS
    IF `the short form applies`
    THEN ((PARTY `the members as a party`
           MAY `s 215D(1) the members resolve by special resolution at a general meeting to approve the amalgamation on the terms`
           HENCE (`s 215E chain: the filing with the Registrar, then the Registrar's notice` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the amalgamated company is a new company` `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`))
          RAND
          (`s 215H chain: the application to the Court, then the order` `the person who applies` `what the person who applies is` `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` `the day of the application to the Court` `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` `the start day of the trace`))
    ELSE ((PARTY `the members as a party`
           MAY `s 215C(1)(a) the members approve the amalgamation proposal by special resolution at a general meeting`
           HENCE (`s 215E chain: the filing with the Registrar, then the Registrar's notice` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the amalgamated company is a new company` `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`))
          RAND
          (`s 215H chain: the application to the Court, then the order` `the person who applies` `what the person who applies is` `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` `the day of the application to the Court` `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` `the start day of the trace`))

§ `The whole chain: the duties before the meeting, then the resolution, the filing, the Registrar and the Court`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the start day of the trace; counting=as in the sections above (every deadline is a backward count from the DATE input of the meeting or of the date of effect)
-- FORK: s 215D(1), (2) | the short form is chosen when the caller's answer from the existing gate `s 215D(1) ...` or `s 215D(2) ...` is JUST TRUE, and the long form otherwise (NOTHING or JUST FALSE) | the long form only on a JUST FALSE
-- FORK: s 215D(1), (2) | the existing gates ask whether "the members ... resolved to approve" on the terms; here that Boolean is the caller's reading of the terms of the resolution proposed, because the chain itself is what brings the resolution about
-- FORK: whole chain | the duties before the meeting and the steps from the resolution are run side by side (RAND) from day 0, and the filing and the Registrar's steps open only on the resolution | the duties before the meeting as a gate on the resolution
-- src:21068 | 215A. Without affecting section 212 and any other law relating to
-- src:21069 | the merger or amalgamation of companies, 2 or more companies may
-- src:21070 | amalgamate and continue as one company, which may be one of the
-- src:21071 | amalgamating companies or a new company, in accordance with
-- src:21072 | sections 215B to 215G, where applicable.
-- src:21510 | (2) An order may be made under subsection (1) on such terms or
-- src:21511 | conditions as the Court thinks fit.
@ref s 215A to s 215H the whole chain of amalgamation (src:21068-21511)
GIVEN `the answer of the short-form gate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name of the amalgamating company` IS A STRING
      `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the members as a party` IS A Party
      `the amalgamating company as a party` IS A Party
      `the amalgamated company is a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person who applies` IS A Party
      `what the person who applies is` IS A `s 215H(1) the person`
      `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application to the Court` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as practicable") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `amalgamation chain act`
`s 215 chain: the whole amalgamation` MEANS
    IF `the answer of the short-form gate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN ((`s 215D chain: the duties before the general meeting` `the name of the amalgamating company` `the name of the director` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace` `the period of all convenient speed, as found`)
          RAND
          (`s 215 chain: the members' resolution, the filing, the Registrar's steps and the Court's power` TRUE `the members as a party` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the amalgamated company is a new company` `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` `the person who applies` `what the person who applies is` `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` `the day of the application to the Court` `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` `the start day of the trace` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`))
    ELSE ((`s 215C chain: the duties before the general meeting` `the name of the amalgamating company` `the name of the director` `the day of the general meeting` `the start day of the trace` `the period of all convenient speed, as found`)
          RAND
          (`s 215 chain: the members' resolution, the filing, the Registrar's steps and the Court's power` FALSE `the members as a party` `the amalgamating company as a party` `the amalgamated company is a new company` `the documents filed are those section 215E(1) requires` `the person who applies` `what the person who applies is` `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person who applies` `the day of the application to the Court` `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` `the start day of the trace` `the period of all convenient speed, as found` `the period the standard of time allows, as found`))
